&lt;p&gt;Choose a local CSV file with a header row and numeric columns. The file is read in your browser and is not uploaded.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;label for="csvFile"&gt;CSV file&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;input id="csvFile" type="file" accept=".csv,text/csv"&gt;
&lt;div id="csvStatus" class="status" style="margin-top:12px"&gt;No file loaded.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;label for="csvColumns"&gt;Variables to include&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;select id="csvColumns" multiple size="6" aria-describedby="csvHelp"&gt;&lt;/select&gt;
&lt;small id="csvHelp"&gt;Select at least two numeric variables. Hold Ctrl (Windows) or Command (Mac) to select multiple columns.&lt;/small&gt;
&lt;label for="csvRow"&gt;Target observation&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;select id="csvRow"&gt;&lt;/select&gt;
&lt;div class="actions"&gt;
  &lt;button id="useCsv"&gt;Use selected CSV data&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button id="downloadDistanceMatrix" class="secondary"&gt;Download distance matrix CSV&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class="muted"&gt;Selected columns define the reference mean and sample covariance. The chosen row becomes the target vector. Rows with missing or non-numeric selected values are excluded from the reference calculation.&lt;/p&gt;







&lt;h2&gt;Result&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;span class="pill" id="state"&gt;Ready to calculate&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;div class="metrics"&gt;
  &lt;div class="metric"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Mahalanobis distance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong id="distance"&gt;—&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="metric"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Squared Mahalanobis distance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong id="squared"&gt;—&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
